+/*
+ * Note FE (0435): Bluetooth step 5, iOS's transport with the bridge in the kernel. `sysctl kern.notefe_bt=8` (root)
+ * does steps 2-4 (UART, power, the chip's patch), then registers the kernel controls an iPhone X's UART Bluetooth has
+ * and starts the bridge thread. The controls and the Skywalk kernel-pipe channel are ios-guacamole's 0220-0222
+ * (sweet_btuart.c, OnePlus 7 Pro; reverse engineering in its research/bluetooth/transport.md): BlueTool connects to
+ * PF_SYSTEM "com.apple.uart.bluetooth", bluetoothd's H4BC transport to "com.apple.uart.sk.bluetooth" and asks it for a
+ * channel (setsockopt 0x800c5414, getsockopt 0x40105412 = nexus UUID, os_channel_create); termios options are kept
+ * and answered. Where guacamole joins them to a userland bridge (btbridge over /dev/pmem, a CPU-polling process), here
+ * the bridge is a kernel thread on UART1 that sleeps 1 ms when there is nothing to move. The chip is a real Broadcom,
+ * so unlike guacamole's Qualcomm almost everything goes to it. Answered here (guacamole's findings, NOTES.md
+ * 2026-11-09): BlueTool's download and link commands (0xfc18 baud, 0xfc2e/0xfc4c/0xfc4e the patch, 0xfc27 sleep mode,
+ * 0xfc45 UART clock: the chip already runs our patch at 115200), LE_Read_Periodic_Advertiser_List_Size 0x204a (it
+ * switches the chip to extended advertising, where bluetoothd's legacy LE scan is refused). Rewritten on the way back:
+ * Read_Local_Version as BlueTool's BCM4357B1 (HCI/LMP 9, manufacturer 0x000f, subversion 0x420e: getChipset picks its
+ * D22 boot script by it), Read_Local_Supported_Commands octet 18 bits 2-3 (Write_Default_Erroneous_Data_Reporting,
+ * which bluetoothd otherwise fails locally), and any Command Complete with status 0x01 (unknown command: Apple's own
+ * vendor commands) turned into success with the first parameter echoed and 15 zero bytes (bcm_vsc.c asserts on a
+ * reply that has only a status). Klog `NOTEFE BT:` (connects, channel, counters every 60 s, the first 40 commands).
+ */
+#include <sys/kern_control.h>
+#include <sys/kpi_mbuf.h>
+#include <sys/termios.h>
+#include <skywalk/os_skywalk_private.h>
+#include <kern/thread.h>
+#include <kern/sched_prim.h>
+
+extern kern_return_t kernel_thread_start(thread_continue_t, void *, thread_t *);
+extern void thread_deallocate(thread_t);
